{
  "id": 3,
  "title": "Family & people",
  "goal": "Talk about your family, say whose something is, and say how many brothers, sisters or children you have.",
  "intro": "Telugu kinship terms are precise: there is no single word for 'brother' or 'sister'. You must say whether they are **older** (*అన్నయ్య*, *అక్క*) or **younger** (*తమ్ముడు*, *చెల్లెలు*) than you, and uncles and aunts differ by which side of the family they are on.\n\nYou will also learn the possessive words (my, your, our) and how Telugu sorts nouns into masculine and non-masculine, which decides the form of the verb.",
